· CC BY-SA 3.0","commercialUse":true,"modifications":"Displayed at responsive sizes; original source linked. Any adapted image remains under the source licence.","specimen":"Emerald","verifiedAt":"2026-10-16","permissionEvidence":"Licence and author checked at the original Commons file page on 2026-10-16. CC BY-SA 3.0; commercial reuse permitted under linked terms. Source-labelled specimen, not independently authenticated.","authenticPhoto":true,"status":"approved","cloudinaryPublicId":"khyatigems-website/reference/2026-10-16/emerald"},"review":{"method":"AI-assisted metadata and visual review","sourceDescription":"Emerald - Muzo Mine - Colombia (Crystal 2cm)","authority":"Owner delegation, 16 October 2026","scope":"Reference photography only; no independent authentication of specimen treatment or origin.","delivery":"Uploaded to ERP-configured Cloudinary; original Commons attribution and licence retained."}},{"slug":"aquamarine","id":"commons-aquamarine","asset":{"title":"Aquamarine (GeoDIL number - 904).jpg","url":"https://res.cloudinary.com/dxu1jawbs/image/upload/v1792155152/khyatigems-website/reference/2026-10-16/aquamarine.jpg","width":960,"height":1237,"alt":"Aquamarine reference photograph, identified by the source.","caption":"Aquamarine reference photograph, identified by the source. Educational example; not KhyatiGems inventory and not an independent treatment or origin assessment.","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aquamarine_(GeoDIL_number_-_904).jpg","creator":"Shannon Heinle","license":"CC0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/deed.en","attribution":"Shannon Heinle · CC0","commercialUse":true,"modifications":"Displayed at responsive sizes; original source linked. Any adapted image remains under the source licence.","specimen":"Aquamarine","verifiedAt":"2026-10-16","permissionEvidence":"Licence and author checked at the original Commons file page on 2026-10-16. CC0; commercial reuse permitted under linked terms. Source-labelled specimen, not independently authenticated.","authenticPhoto":true,"status":"approved","cloudinaryPublicId":"khyatigems-website/reference/2026-10-16/aquamarine"},"review":{"method":"AI-assisted metadata and visual review","sourceDescription":"Aquamarine Be3Al2Si6O18 is the blue to blue-green or aqua variety of the mineral beryl. Aquamarine is colored by trace amounts of iron that find their way into the crystal structure. The environment that beryl is found in is mostly granitic pegmatites. Gem aquamarines can be heat treated to produce a more desireable color from lesser pale colored stones. Its name comes from the ancient Greek, beryllos, signifying a “precious blue-green color of sea water” stone.","authority":"Owner delegation, 16 October 2026","scope":"Reference photography only; no independent authentication of specimen treatment or origin.","delivery":"Uploaded to ERP-configured Cloudinary; original Commons attribution and licence retained."}},{"slug":"amethyst","id":"commons-amethyst","asset":{"title":"Amethyst crystals close.jpg","url":"https://res.cloudinary.com/dxu1jawbs/image/upload/v1792155154/khyatigems-website/reference/2026-10-16/amethyst.jpg","width":960,"height":640,"alt":"Amethyst reference photograph, identified by the source.","caption":"Amethyst reference photograph, identified by the source. Educational example; not KhyatiGems inventory and not an independent treatment or origin assessment.","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Amethyst_crystals_close.jpg","creator":"Lisa Ann Yount","license":"CC0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/deed.en","attribution":"Lisa Ann Yount · CC0","commercialUse":true,"modifications":"Displayed at responsive sizes; original source linked. Any adapted image remains under the source licence.","specimen":"Amethyst","verifiedAt":"2026-10-16","permissionEvidence":"Licence and author checked at the original Commons file page on 2026-10-16. CC0; commercial reuse permitted under linked terms. Source-labelled specimen, not independently authenticated.","authenticPhoto":true,"status":"approved","cloudinaryPublicId":"khyatigems-website/reference/2026-10-16/amethyst"},"review":{"method":"AI-assisted metadata and visual review","sourceDescription":"Amethyst crystals","authority":"Owner delegation, 16 October 2026","scope":"Reference photography only; no independent authentication of specimen treatment or origin.","delivery":"Uploaded to ERP-configured Cloudinary; original Commons attribution and licence retained."}},{"slug":"citrine","id":"commons-citrine","asset":{"title":"Rough Citrine Cristals Quartz from Brasil.jpg","url":"https://res.cloudinary.com/dxu1jawbs/image/upload/v1792155156/khyatigems-website/reference/2026-10-16/citrine.jpg","width":960,"height":540,"alt":"Citrine reference photograph, identified by the source.","caption":"Citrine reference photograph, identified by the source. Educational example; not KhyatiGems inventory and not an independent treatment or origin assessment.","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rough_Citrine_Cristals_Quartz_from_Brasil.jpg","creator":"Paweł Maliszczak [hardleo.com]","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","attribution":"Paweł Maliszczak [hardleo.com] · CC BY-SA 4.0","commercialUse":true,"modifications":"Displayed at responsive sizes; original source linked. Any adapted image remains under the source licence.","specimen":"Citrine","verifiedAt":"2026-10-16","permissionEvidence":"Licence and author checked at the original Commons file page on 2026-10-16. CC BY-SA 4.0; commercial reuse permitted under linked terms. Source-labelled specimen, not independently authenticated.","authenticPhoto":true,"status":"approved","cloudinaryPublicId":"khyatigems-website/reference/2026-10-16/citrine"},"review":{"method":"AI-assisted metadata and visual review","sourceDescription":"Rough Citrine Crystals Quartz from Brasil","authority":"Owner delegation, 16 October 2026","scope":"Reference photography only; no independent authentication of specimen treatment or origin.","delivery":"Uploaded to ERP-configured Cloudinary; original Commons attribution and licence retained."}},{"slug":"peridot","id":"commons-peridot","asset":{"title":"Peridot (GeoDIL number - 1027).jpg","url":"https://res.cloudinary.com/dxu1jawbs/image/upload/v1792155159/khyatigems-website/reference/2026-10-16/peridot.jpg","width":960,"height":764,"alt":"Peridot reference photograph, identified by the source.","caption":"Peridot reference photograph, identified by the source. Educational example; not KhyatiGems inventory and not an independent treatment or origin assessment.","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Peridot_(GeoDIL_number_-_1027).jpg","creator":"Darla Sondrol","license":"CC0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/deed.en","attribution":"Darla Sondrol · CC0","commercialUse":true,"modifications":"Displayed at responsive sizes; original source linked. Any adapted image remains under the source licence.","specimen":"Peridot","verifiedAt":"2026-10-16","permissionEvidence":"Licence and author checked at the original Commons file page on 2026-10-16. CC0; commercial reuse permitted under linked terms. Source-labelled specimen, not independently authenticated.","authenticPhoto":true,"status":"approved","cloudinaryPublicId":"khyatigems-website/reference/2026-10-16/peridot"},"review":{"method":"AI-assisted metadata and visual review","sourceDescription":"Peridot (pronounced pair-a-doe) is the gem variety of olivine. Olivine, is a general name used for minerals of the fayalite (Fe2SiO4) - forsterite (Mg2SiO4) series, so olivine's formula is written as (Mg,Fe)2SiO4. Peridot is usually closer to forsterite than fayalite in composition although iron is the coloring agent for peridot. The best colored peridot has an iron percentage of less than 15% and includes nickel and chromium as trace elements that may also contribute to the best peridot color. The largest crystal shown is about 1.5 cm across.","authority":"Owner delegation, 16 October 2026","scope":"Reference photography only; no independent authentication of specimen treatment or origin.","delivery":"Uploaded to ERP-configured Cloudinary; original Commons attribution and licence retained."}},{"slug":"topaz","id":"commons-topaz","asset":{"title":"Topaze.jpg","url":"https://res.cloudinary.com/dxu1jawbs/image/upload/v1792155161/khyatigems-website/reference/2026-10-16/topaz.jpg","width":960,"height":638,"alt":"Topaz reference photograph, identified by the source.","caption":"Topaz reference photograph, identified by the source. Educational example; not KhyatiGems inventory and not an independent treatment or origin assessment.","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Topaze.jpg","creator":"Parent Géry","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","attribution":"Parent Géry · CC BY-SA 3.0","commercialUse":true,"modifications":"Displayed at responsive sizes; original source linked. Any adapted image remains under the source licence.","specimen":"Topaz","verifiedAt":"2026-10-16","permissionEvidence":"Licence and author checked at the original Commons file page on 2026-10-16. CC BY-SA 3.0; commercial reuse permitted under linked terms. Source-labelled specimen, not independently authenticated.","authenticPhoto":true,"status":"approved","cloudinaryPublicId":"khyatigems-website/reference/2026-10-16/topaz"},"review":{"method":"AI-assisted metadata and visual review","sourceDescription":"crystal of topaz : Yuno (Yunau ; Yunas), Shigar Valley, Skardu District, Baltistan, Gilgit-Baltistan (Northern Areas), Pakistan - crystal : 20 mm","authority":"Owner delegation, 16 October 2026","scope":"Reference photography only; no independent authentication of specimen treatment or origin.","delivery":"Uploaded to ERP-configured Cloudinary; original Commons attribution and licence retained."}},{"slug":"spinel","id":"commons-spinel","asset":{"title":"Calcite-Spinel-dtn37a.jpg","url":"https://res.cloudinary.com/dxu1jawbs/image/upload/v1792155163/khyatigems-website/reference/2026-10-16/spinel.jpg","width":288,"height":449,"alt":"Spinel crystals associated with calcite, as labelled by the source.","caption":"Spinel crystals associated with calcite, as labelled by the source. Educational example; not KhyatiGems inventory and not an independent treatment or origin assessment.","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Calcite-Spinel-dtn37a.jpg","creator":"Robert M. Lavinsky","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","attribution":"Robert M. Lavinsky · CC BY-SA 3.0","commercialUse":true,"modifications":"Displayed at responsive sizes; original source linked. Any adapted image remains under the source licence.","specimen":"Spinel","verifiedAt":"2026-10-16","permissionEvidence":"Licence and author checked at the original Commons file page on 2026-10-16. CC BY-SA 3.0; commercial reuse permitted under linked terms. Source-labelled specimen, not independently authenticated.","authenticPhoto":true,"status":"approved","cloudinaryPublicId":"khyatigems-website/reference/2026-10-16/spinel"},"review":{"method":"AI-assisted metadata and visual review","sourceDescription":"Calcite, Spinel Locality: Mogok, Pyin Oo Lwin District, Mandalay Division, Burma (Myanmar) (Locality at mindat.org) Size: thumbnail, 1.5 x 1.1 x 1 cm Spinel on Calcite Without question, this vivid red, gemmy, octahedron of spinel on white calcite, is a world class competition thumbnail. Most Mogok spinels are simply loose singles, off matrix. This one, carefully excavated from a miniature at Bill Larson's lab by Irv, is unrepaired and remains on matrix due to the careful prep work. You almost never see this quality of crystal , aside from the additional aesthetics of it being on matrix! The well formed , complete crystal measures .8 cm across. It is truly a thing of beauty.","authority":"Owner delegation, 16 October 2026","scope":"Reference photography only; no independent authentication of specimen treatment or origin.","delivery":"Uploaded to ERP-configured Cloudinary; original Commons attribution and licence retained."}},{"slug":"garnet","id":"commons-garnet","asset":{"title":"Garnet 06.jpg","url":"https://res.cloudinary.com/dxu1jawbs/image/upload/v1792155166/khyatigems-website/reference/2026-10-16/garnet.jpg","width":960,"height":638,"alt":"Garnet reference photograph, identified by the source.","caption":"Garnet reference photograph, identified by the source. Educational example; not KhyatiGems inventory and not an independent treatment or origin assessment.","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Garnet_06.jpg","creator":"Géry PARENT","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","attribution":"Géry PARENT · CC BY-SA 3.0","commercialUse":true,"modifications":"Displayed at responsive sizes; original source linked. Any adapted image remains under the source licence.","specimen":"Garnet","verifiedAt":"2026-10-16","permissionEvidence":"Licence and author checked at the original Commons file page on 2026-10-16. CC BY-SA 3.0; commercial reuse permitted under linked terms. Source-labelled specimen, not independently authenticated.","authenticPhoto":true,"status":"approved","cloudinaryPublicId":"khyatigems-website/reference/2026-10-16/garnet"},"review":{"method":"AI-assisted metadata and visual review","sourceDescription":"garnet var. grossular : Sierra de Cruces, Mun. de Sierra Mojada, Coahuila, Mexico","authority":"Owner delegation, 16 October 2026","scope":"Reference photography only; no independent authentication of specimen treatment or origin.","delivery":"Uploaded to ERP-configured Cloudinary; original Commons attribution and licence retained."}},{"slug":"tourmaline","id":"commons-tourmaline","asset":{"title":"Pale watermel