ot KhyatiGems inventory and not an independent treatment or origin assessment.","sourceUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Zircon-dtn1a.jpg","creator":"Robert M. Lavinsky","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","attribution":"Robert M. Lavinsky · CC BY-SA 3.0","commercialUse":true,"modifications":"Displayed at responsive sizes; original source linked. Any adapted image remains under the source licence.","specimen":"Zircon","verifiedAt":"2026-10-16","permissionEvidence":"Licence and author checked at the original Commons file page on 2026-10-16. CC BY-SA 3.0; commercial reuse permitted under linked terms. Source-labelled specimen, not independently authenticated.","authenticPhoto":true,"status":"approved","cloudinaryPublicId":"khyatigems-website/reference/2026-10-16/zircon"},"review":{"method":"AI-assisted metadata and visual review","sourceDescription":"Zircon Locality: Gilgit, Gilgit District, Northern Areas, Pakistan (Locality at mindat.org) Size: thumbnail, 1.8 x 1.5 x 1.1 cm Zircon This is a lustrous, gemmy, cognac-colored crystal of zircon perched on a sugary, tan matrix of calcite. The tetragonal form of the almost, 1.0 cm zircon crystal, is very evident. It is a superb thumbnail, and of a quality that is extremely rare for the locality - let alone in an aesthetic specimen of any kind! This complex crystal is stunning.","authority":"Owner delegation, 16 October 2026","scope":"Reference photography only; no independent authentication of specimen treatment or origin.","delivery":"Uploaded to ERP-configured Cloudinary; original Commons attribution and licence retained."}},{"slug":"tanzanite","id":"commons-tanzanite","asset":{"title":"Rough Tanzanite Gemstone from Mirerani.jpg","url":"https://res.cloudinary.com/dxu1jawbs/image/upload/v1792155174/khyatigems-website/reference/2026-10-16/tanzanite.jpg","width":960,"height":720,"alt":"Tanzanite reference photograph, identified by the source.","caption":"Tanzani